{"content_hash": "bc4657fa2f83c84d", "version_id": 332, "article_id": 34, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Scientists Fix a Small Name Mistake in a Big Study", "title_zh": "科学家更正大研究中的一个小名字错误", "has_translation": true, "topic": "science", "source": "nature", "source_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-11266-0", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1710447503692-8364152e431c?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8YXV0aG9yJTIwY29ycmVjdGlvbnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNTUwMzAwfDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Benja Godin on Unsplash", "author": "Benja Godin", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@benja_godin?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-person-writing-on-a-piece-of-paper-with-a-pen-SgZ6nWHi8FY?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(212, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(250, 46%, 48%)", "label": "SCIENCE", "seed": "14846e897d91"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 194, "reading_minutes": 1.0, "lead": "A team of scientists published a study about our immune system. Later, they found a small mistake in one author's name. They wrote a correction to fix it.", "lead_zh": "一个科学家团队发表了一项关于我们免疫系统的研究。后来，他们发现一位作者的名字有个小错误。他们写了一篇更正来修正它。", "preview": "On 30 September 2026, a group of scientists published a study in the journal Nature. The study is about how our bodies fight disease. It loo", "preview_zh": "2026年9月30日，一组科学家在《自然》杂志上发表了一项研究。这项研究是关于我们的身体如何对抗疾病的。它研究了一种叫做MLLT1和MLLT3的特殊蛋白质。这些蛋白质帮助控制一种叫做AID的重要酶。科学家们想了解AID在我们的细胞中是如何工作的。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 329, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/34/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 85.525, "size_bytes": 516816, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 227, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@09df8a5/content/data/versions/332.json", "paragraphs": ["On 30 September 2026, a group of scientists published a study in the journal Nature. The study is about how our bodies fight disease. It looks at special proteins called MLLT1 and MLLT3. These proteins help control an important enzyme called AID. The scientists wanted to understand how AID works in our cells.", "Later, the scientists found a small problem. One author's last name was spelled wrong. His name is Marcelo A. Navarrete. In the first version, it was written as 'Navarrette' with an extra 'r'. The team corrected this mistake in the online and PDF versions of the article.", "On 8 October 2026, Nature published an Author Correction. This is a short note that fixes the mistake. The correction tells readers the correct spelling of the author's name. Many authors worked on this study. They come from universities in Canada and Chile. The main author is Javier M. Di Noia.", "This correction is important because it makes the record correct. Scientists often publish corrections when they find small errors. It helps everyone trust the research. The original study was published on 30 September 2026. The correction came out just over a week later."], "paragraphs_zh": ["2026年9月30日，一组科学家在《自然》杂志上发表了一项研究。这项研究是关于我们的身体如何对抗疾病的。它研究了一种叫做MLLT1和MLLT3的特殊蛋白质。这些蛋白质帮助控制一种叫做AID的重要酶。科学家们想了解AID在我们的细胞中是如何工作的。", "后来，科学家们发现了一个小问题。一位作者的姓氏拼写错了。他的名字是Marcelo A. Navarrete。在第一个版本中，它被写成了'Navarrette'，多了一个'r'。团队在文章的在线版和PDF版中更正了这个错误。", "2026年10月8日，《自然》杂志发布了一篇作者更正。这是一个修正错误的小说明。更正告诉读者作者名字的正确拼写。许多作者参与了这项研究。他们来自加拿大和智利的大学。主要作者是Javier M. Di Noia。", "这个更正很重要，因为它使记录正确。科学家们经常在发现小错误时发布更正。它帮助每个人信任这项研究。原始研究发表于2026年9月30日。更正仅在一周多后发布。"], "body": "On 30 September 2026, a group of scientists published a study in the journal Nature. The study is about how our bodies fight disease. It looks at special proteins called MLLT1 and MLLT3. These proteins help control an important enzyme called AID. The scientists wanted to understand how AID works in our cells.\n\nLater, the scientists found a small problem. One author's last name was spelled wrong. His name is Marcelo A. Navarrete. In the first version, it was written as 'Navarrette' with an extra 'r'. The team corrected this mistake in the online and PDF versions of the article.\n\nOn 8 October 2026, Nature published an Author Correction. This is a short note that fixes the mistake. The correction tells readers the correct spelling of the author's name. Many authors worked on this study. They come from universities in Canada and Chile. The main author is Javier M. Di Noia.\n\nThis correction is important because it makes the record correct. Scientists often publish corrections when they find small errors. It helps everyone trust the research. The original study was published on 30 September 2026. The correction came out just over a week later.", "body_zh": "2026年9月30日，一组科学家在《自然》杂志上发表了一项研究。这项研究是关于我们的身体如何对抗疾病的。它研究了一种叫做MLLT1和MLLT3的特殊蛋白质。这些蛋白质帮助控制一种叫做AID的重要酶。科学家们想了解AID在我们的细胞中是如何工作的。\n\n后来，科学家们发现了一个小问题。一位作者的姓氏拼写错了。他的名字是Marcelo A. Navarrete。在第一个版本中，它被写成了'Navarrette'，多了一个'r'。团队在文章的在线版和PDF版中更正了这个错误。\n\n2026年10月8日，《自然》杂志发布了一篇作者更正。这是一个修正错误的小说明。更正告诉读者作者名字的正确拼写。许多作者参与了这项研究。他们来自加拿大和智利的大学。主要作者是Javier M. Di Noia。\n\n这个更正很重要，因为它使记录正确。科学家们经常在发现小错误时发布更正。它帮助每个人信任这项研究。原始研究发表于2026年9月30日。更正仅在一周多后发布。", "text": "On 30 September 2026, a group of scientists published a study in the journal Nature. The study is about how our bodies fight disease. It looks at special proteins called MLLT1 and MLLT3. These proteins help control an important enzyme called AID. The scientists wanted to understand how AID works in our cells. Later, the scientists found a small problem. One author's last name was spelled wrong. His name is Marcelo A. Navarrete. In the first version, it was written as 'Navarrette' with an extra 'r'. The team corrected this mistake in the online and PDF versions of the article. On 8 October 2026, Nature published an Author Correction. This is a short note that fixes the mistake. The correction tells readers the correct spelling of the author's name. Many authors worked on this study. They come from universities in Canada and Chile. The main author is Javier M. Di Noia. This correction is important because it makes the record correct. Scientists often publish corrections when they find small errors. It helps everyone trust the research. The original study was published on 30 September 2026. The correction came out just over a week later.", "vocab": [{"word": "scientist", "pos": "noun", "zh": "科学家", "note": ""}, {"word": "study", "pos": "noun", "zh": "研究", "note": "也可以作动词，表示“学习”或“研究”"}, {"word": "publish", "pos": "verb", "zh": "发表", "note": "常用被动语态"}, {"word": "author", "pos": "noun", "zh": "作者", "note": ""}, {"word": "correction", "pos": "noun", "zh": "更正", "note": "动词是 correct"}, {"word": "mistake", "pos": "noun", "zh": "错误", "note": ""}, {"word": "name", "pos": "noun", "zh": "名字", "note": ""}, {"word": "journal", "pos": "noun", "zh": "期刊", "note": "例如 Nature 是一本期刊"}], "title_original": "Author Correction: Histone readers MLLT1 and MLLT3 concentrate AID to confer locus specificity", "summary_original": "Nature, Published online: 08 October 2026;\ndoi:10.1038/s41586-026-11266-0\nAuthor Correction: Histone readers MLLT1 and MLLT3 concentrate AID to confer locus specificity", "body_original": "Download PDF\nAuthor Correction\nPublished:\n08 October 2026\nAuthor Correction: Histone readers MLLT1 and MLLT3 concentrate AID to confer locus specificity\nNoé Seija\nORCID:\norcid.org/0000-0003-2223-1291\n1\n,\n2\n,\nSophia Gannon\n1\n,\n3\nna1\n,\nKíra A. Häfner\nORCID:\norcid.org/0009-0008-1069-4647\n1\n,\n2\nna1\n,\nTim M. Gemeinhardt\nORCID:\norcid.org/0000-0003-0241-1009\n1\n,\n4\nna1\n,\nJana Ridani\n1\n,\n4\n,\nDiego Alvarez\nORCID:\norcid.org/0000-0003-0753-274X\n5\n,\nMélanie Provencher\n1\n,\n6\n,\nPoorani Ganesh Subramani\nORCID:\norcid.org/0000-0002-7318-6577\n1\n,\nChristian Poitras\nORCID:\norcid.org/00